Let me now write the instrument. Design details:

**Text extraction**: build a canonical string per review from: statement, summary, note, delta_vs_draft, findings (list of strings or dicts; recursively stringify), reason, comments, rationale, does_not_claim, next_falsifier. Exclude metadata noise (event_id, hashes, timestamps, score). Normalize: lowercase, replace hex tokens with `<hex>`, digits with `<n>`, whitespace collapse, strip punctuation. Then 4-gram word shingles.

Wait — excluding hashes but including findings. Also note many reviews only differ by target hash numbers. Normalizing numbers to `<n>` helps detect templates.

**Similarity**: Jaccard on shingle sets. If text length < 20 tokens, use token-set Jaccard. Single-linkage clustering at threshold T=0.5 default; report sweep T ∈ {0.3,0.4,0.5,0.6,0.7}.

**Reviewer identity**: `reviewer` field (strip parenthetical), else `actor`. Normalize: lowercase, strip "(...)", strip trailing role words. Report `actor` distinct count too.

